.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt PAZARI-STRESS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazari-stress
.Nd deterministic memory workload generator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -arena Ar size
.Op Fl -cache-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -fill Cm index | random
.Op Fl -interval Ar duration
.Op Fl -no-reserve
.Op Fl -no-thp
.Ar phase ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
allocates and frees memory according to a plan given on the command line, and
writes a JSON record of its progress to standard output.
It is intended for testing
.Xr pazari-agent 1
and
.Xr pazarid 1 .
.Pp
The tool maps a single anonymous region, the arena, at startup.
It tracks a frontier: the offset below which pages are resident.
Each phase moves the frontier or leaves it in place:
.Bl -tag -width "release" -offset indent
.It Cm grow
Advance the frontier, faulting in each page it passes.
.It Cm release
Move the frontier back, dropping pages with
.Dv MADV_DONTNEED .
.It Cm churn
Rewrite resident pages without moving the frontier.
.It Cm hold
Do nothing for a time.
.It Cm cache
Grow the page cache by writing a scratch file.
.El
.Pp
The tool is single-threaded and allocates nothing beyond the plan, so a phase
that stops progressing is being held back by the kernel.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -arena Ar size
Size of the arena.
Defaults to the plan's peak frontier.
Required if the plan never grows.
.It Fl -cache-dir Ar dir
Where
.Cm cache
phases write.
Required if the plan has a
.Cm cache
phase.
Use a disk-backed filesystem: on tmpfs the file is shared memory, not page
cache.
.It Fl -fill Cm index | random
What to write into each page.
.Cm index ,
the default, writes one word per page.
.Cm random
fills each page with pseudo-random data, which a compressed swap device such as
zram cannot shrink.
.It Fl -interval Ar duration
How often a running phase reports progress.
Default
.Cm 500ms .
.It Fl -no-reserve
Map the arena with
.Dv MAP_NORESERVE ,
so it is not charged to
.Va Committed_AS
when mapped.
.It Fl -no-thp
Exclude the arena from transparent huge pages with
.Dv MADV_NOHUGEPAGE .
.El
.Sh PHASES
Each
.Ar phase
is a kind, a target, and optional
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
grow=SIZE[,rate=SIZE/s][,chunk=SIZE]
release=SIZE[,rate=SIZE/s][,chunk=SIZE]
churn=DURATION,rate=SIZE/s[,chunk=SIZE]
hold=DURATION
cache=SIZE[,rate=SIZE/s][,chunk=SIZE]
.Ed
.Pp
Phases run in order.
.Cm rate
limits throughput and is required for
.Cm churn .
Without it, a phase runs as fast as it can.
.Cm chunk
is how much memory is moved between rate checks.
It defaults to 1MiB for
.Cm grow ,
.Cm churn
and
.Cm cache ,
and 64MiB for
.Cm release .
.Pp
Sizes and durations are written as in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
Zero is not allowed for any size, rate or chunk.
.Pp
The whole plan is checked before anything is mapped.
A plan that releases below the start of the arena, churns an empty arena, or
grows past the arena is rejected.
.Pp
A
.Cm grow
faults in every page it touches, including a partial final page.
A
.Cm release
drops every page wholly above the new frontier.
The page the frontier ends in stays resident.
A
.Cm cache
syncs what it writes, so the page cache it leaves is clean.
.Sh OUTPUT
Events are written to standard output as one JSON object per line; logs go to
standard error.
Every event has a
.Va type
field.
Byte counts are integers, and
.Va elapsed_ms
is milliseconds since the process started, from a monotonic clock.
.Pp
A run writes one
.Cm started
event, then for each phase one
.Cm phase ,
zero or more
.Cm progress
and one
.Cm completed ,
and finally one of
.Cm done ,
.Cm interrupted
or
.Cm failed .
An interruption or failure ends the stream early.
.Bl -tag -width "interrupted"
.It Cm started
.Va pid ,
.Va page_size ,
.Va arena
(rounded up to a page),
.Va no_reserve ,
.Va no_thp ,
.Va fill ,
.Va cache_dir
if set,
and
.Va plan ,
an array of the parsed phases.
Each phase has
.Va spec ,
.Va kind ,
.Va target_bytes
or
.Va target_ms ,
.Va chunk ,
and
.Va rate_bps
if set.
.It Cm phase
.Va index
(from 0),
.Va kind ,
and
.Va target_bytes
for
.Cm grow ,
.Cm release
and
.Cm cache ,
or
.Va target_ms
for
.Cm churn
and
.Cm hold .
.It Cm progress
.Va index ,
.Va elapsed_ms ,
.Va touched
(bytes moved so far in this phase; 0 for
.Cm hold ) ,
.Va frontier ,
and
.Va rate_bps
since the previous report.
A phase shorter than
.Fl -interval
reports no progress.
.It Cm completed
.Va index ,
.Va elapsed_ms .
.It Cm done
.Va elapsed_ms .
.It Cm interrupted
.Va index
of the running phase and
.Va elapsed_ms ,
after
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT .
.It Cm failed
.Va elapsed_ms
and
.Va error ,
a human-readable message.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RUST_LOG
Log filter, in
.Va tracing-subscriber
.Va EnvFilter
syntax.
Defaults to
.Cm info .
Does not affect the event stream.
.It Ev JOURNAL_STREAM
Set by systemd.
When it refers to standard error, logs go to the journal directly, with
structured fields prefixed
.Cm F_ .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The run ended with
.Cm done
or
.Cm interrupted .
.It 1
The run ended with
.Cm failed .
So does an invalid plan or option value.
.It 2
The options could not be parsed.
No events were written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Grow to 2GiB, hold, then return most of it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pazari-stress --no-reserve \e
    grow=2GiB,rate=384MiB/s hold=30s release=1536MiB hold=60s
.Ed
.Pp
Allocate as fast as possible, to test the brake:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pazari-stress --arena 4GiB grow=200MiB,rate=200MiB/s grow=3GiB hold=300s
.Ed
.Pp
Use incompressible pages, for guests with zram:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pazari-stress --fill random --no-thp grow=1GiB,rate=128MiB/s hold=120s
.Ed
.Pp
Show only progress events:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pazari-stress grow=1GiB hold=10s | jq -c 'select(.type == "progress")'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pazari-agent 1 ,
.Xr pazarid 1 ,
.Xr madvise 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr pazari 7
